{"author":{"id":"ad87ffa09351c4e5a412ec8ee1546e86b314f33d6f28629bb4bcfe7b2290924d"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794624043,"nonce":"BOZf51/fep2N8R4Akx1R7RTp5U8=","title":"Annotations: an entry's user attaches something to a range of its text (first kind: audio, as an external URL), seen wherever the entry is seen. Storage is generic (a kind and JSON data); each kind's shape and rendering are code. First use: the narration for the 40 Storybooks Poland stories in curated/pl (#71).","message":"Decided:\n- Annotations belong to an entry (user_document), not to the shared document. Only the entry's user adds or removes them. Another user importing the same text doesn't get them.\n- Standoff, not markup in the text: a document's id is a hash of its text, so annotations live beside it and adding one doesn't make a new document or touch the analysis.\n- Anchored by a character range [start, end) in UTF-16 units (as JavaScript counts), not by paragraph/sentence/token index, which depend on the analyzer. The bundle's token offsets are code points (separate git-bug item to move them to UTF-16); they're the same for Polish but differ outside the BMP.\n- Audio is an external URL for now, not hosted by us.\n- Not in the analysis bundle: fetched separately, so no BUNDLER_VERSION bump.\n\n\n    -- Something an entry's user attached to a range of its text, seen wherever the entry is: a\n    -- recording of a paragraph, say. start and end are UTF-16 offsets into the text, as\n    -- JavaScript counts them; a document's text never changes, so they never go stale. kind\n    -- names what data holds: the API checks data against that kind's schema\n    -- (shared/annotations.ts), and the reader skips a kind it doesn't know. An annotation has\n    -- its own credit, since a recording's narrator and licence aren't the text's. id is a hash\n    -- of what the annotation says, so the same one added twice is one row and a changed one is new.\n    CREATE TABLE user_document_annotation (\n      user_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n      document_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n      id TEXT NOT NULL,\n      start INTEGER NOT NULL CHECK (start \u003e= 0),\n      \"end\" INTEGER NOT NULL CHECK (\"end\" \u003e start),\n      kind TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (kind GLOB '[a-z]*' AND kind NOT GLOB '*[^a-z0-9-]*'),\n      data TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (json_valid(data) AND json_type(data) = 'object'),\n      licence TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (licence IN ('public-domain', 'cc0', 'cc-by', 'cc-by-sa', 'cc-by-nc', 'cc-by-nc-sa', 'cc-by-nd', 'cc-by-nc-nd')),\n      author TEXT,\n      source TEXT CHECK (source GLOB 'http://?*' OR source GLOB 'https://?*'),\n      added_at TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (added_at IS strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ', added_at)),\n      PRIMARY KEY (user_id, document_id, id),\n      FOREIGN KEY (user_id, document_id) REFERENCES user_document (user_id, document_id) ON DELETE CASCADE\n    ) STRICT, WITHOUT ROWID;\n\n    -- An entry's annotations in order, a page at a time\n    CREATE INDEX user_document_annotation_start_idx ON user_document_annotation (user_id, document_id, start, id);\n\nNotes:\n- Licence is shareable values only, so making an entry public never meets an annotation that can't be shared. Once the licence-table item lands it becomes a foreign key like user_document.licence.\n- Deleting a user or entry deletes its annotations (cascade), as with user_document_tag.\n- end within the text, and data matching its kind, can't be checked in SQL (the text is in R2, textKey in shared/keys.ts); the API checks both.\n- id: sha256 hex of a canonical JSON of {start, end, kind, data, licence, author, source}, so adding the same annotation twice is a no-op.\n- Follow migrations 0007/0008 for style; api/src/migrations.test.ts covers migrations.\n\n\nA registry from kind to a Zod schema of its data. Start with one:\n\n    audio: z.strictObject({ url: https URL })\n\nA new kind is an entry here plus a renderer in the reader; no migration. Export the kind union and a parse that returns null for an unknown kind (the reader skips those, so an old reader keeps working).\n\n\nFollow how entry tags work (api/src/controllers/documents.ts, DocumentStore in api/src/ports.ts, D1 adapter in api/src/worker/adapters.ts, schemas in shared/schemas.ts, types in shared/api.ts).\n\n- GET /api/documents/:id/annotations: the annotations of the entry the viewer sees for the text, chosen as DocumentStore.visible chooses it (their own, else the earliest public one), so they match the title and credit shown. Paged by cursor on (start, id), like the other list endpoints (shared/page.ts, #66). 404 as GET /api/documents/:id does.\n- POST /api/documents/:id/annotations: adds to the caller's own entry; 404 if they have none. Body: start, end, kind, data, licence, author?, source?. Check data against the kind, end \u003c= the text's UTF-16 length, licence shareable. Returns the annotation with its id. Adding an existing one is fine (same id).\n- DELETE /api/documents/:id/annotations/:annotationId: from the caller's own entry.\n- Add these to DocumentStore and the D1 adapter; a per-entry cap on how many annotations (plan for scale).\n- Tests through the typed client: client(app, headers), body(), expectStatus() (src/testing). Cover: someone else's public entry's annotations are visible; a private entry's aren't to others; only the entry's user can add/delete; unknown kind, bad data, end past the text and non-shareable licence are 400; pages.\n\n\n- api/src/curated-kinds.ts: an optional annotations list on both kinds. Each item: paragraph (1-based, paragraphs split on blank lines of the text as resolved) or start/end, plus kind, data, licence, author?, source?. Resolve paragraphs to UTF-16 offsets of the paragraph's text (without the blank lines). Fail the file if a paragraph doesn't exist or data doesn't match its kind (offline check, curated.test.ts, where possible).\n- api/src/sync-curated.ts: plan annotations per text by id, as documents are by id: add the missing ones, delete the ones no longer in the file. List them in --check.\n- check-curated.ts (#72) resolves annotations too.\n\n\nFor each curated/pl file whose source is https://global-asp.github.io/storybooks-poland/stories/pl/\u003cNNNN\u003e/, paragraph n's narration is https://globalstorybooks.net/media/audio/pl/\u003cNNNN\u003e/mp3/\u003cn+1 as 2 digits\u003e.mp3 (01.mp3 is the title). Every one of the 40 stories has exactly one clip per page plus the title clip, and each page is one paragraph in our files. Narrator for all 40: Helena Gabriela (author of each annotation). Source: the story page.\nOpen: the story pages have one CC notice for \"this work\" and nothing for the recordings separately; the site footer is CC BY 4.0. Ask the user which licence the annotations get before adding them.\n\n\n- Fetch the annotations alongside the text (TanStack Query, as the rest of the reader's API state).\n- First renderer: audio, a play button at the start of each annotated range, playing the URL in an \u003caudio\u003e element. Narrator and licence link in the credit line, as the text's are.\n- Map a range to the pieces it overlaps by UTF-16 offset.\n- Screenshots in the PR at 1280 and 390 px (CLAUDE.md), against a preview with the curated audio.\n\n\nOne PR for 1-3 (migration, kinds, API, tests); one for 4-5 (curated + sync + audio files, after the licence question); one for 6 (reader). Run just e2e and just screenshot before calling a PR done.","files":null}]}